== Loadouts ==
Loadouts are previously saved character templates, or presets, of race and multi-class combinations. Loadouts are accessed from the '''Loadouts''' tab on the Inventory screen. Loadouts may only be changed within certain zones: cities and zones adjacent to cities with a "newbie area".  As noted above, after level 11 your race and primary class cannot be changed until you unlock other options.  Secondary and Tertiary classes may be changed at will.  Loadouts are intended to allow you to save commonly used combinations for rapid swapping when in a zone where your loadout may be changed.

NOTE: If you copy equipment from one loadout to an existing loadout, and you are wondering where some of your items in the latter went, check your '''Storage -> Equipment''' tab on the Inventory screen.

== Leveling Classes ==
Up to level 10, all 16 classes will level at the same time, regardless of which combination you are actively playing. Beginning at level 10, ''only'' the classes you are actively playing will gain experience, and at they do so at the same rate. If at any time you switch to a different loadout, or edit your current loadout, your character level will be adjusted to the ''lowest'' of the three classes that you chose.  Also in this case, only the lowest class will gain experience.  If two classes are at equal level, but lower than the third, then both lower classes will gain experience.  If all three are the same level, then all three will gain experience.

== Alternate Advancement (AA) ==
[[Alternate Advancement]] (AA) is an additional form of character progression that is (mostly) independent of your Loadout.  They are accessed via the '''Alternate Advancement''' section of your character screen (default hotkey v).  In general, they are various additional abilities or passive buffs which will be applied to your character when unlocked.  Certain AAs are automatically unlocked for certain classes.  Most will be unlocked by earning AA points to spend on the various AAs you decide would be beneficial to you.  AA points are earned similarly to character levels in that you gain AA experience from killing mobs and questing.  You will earn this experience alongside and simultaneously to your leveling experience.  Once purchased and unlocked, AAs will apply to your character across all loadouts for general AAs.  If an AA has a class requirement, it will only be active if an appropriate class is in your current Loadout.  Disabled AAs are not lost; they will remain dormant and reactivate when an appropriate class is loaded.

AAs are also organized into three broad categories: General, Archetype, and Class.  General AAs are available to everyone in all loadouts.  Archetype AAs apply to certain broad categories of classes, such as meelee dps, tanks, casters, etc.  Naturally, Class AAs are specific to each class.  As noted above, AAs that require a class you do not currently have loaded will be disabled until an appropriate class is active.

Of note, AA experience appears to be earned faster as lower levels than higher levels.  As such if you want to maximize the number of AA points you will eventually earn, then you should attempt to always be leveling one class at a time, i.e. have one class in your loadout be lower than both of the others, as much as possible.  If such min-maxing doesn't appeal to you, then don't worry.  You'll still get plenty of AA points even if you do not strictly follow this recommendation.

== Leveling Zones ==

While there is no one best place to level, many of the [[Updated Zones]] offer a better leveling experience, as well as updated and improved gear.  The [[Recommended Levels and ZEM List]] also provides for a visual guide of zones and levels ranges.

== Frequently Asked Questions ==

'''Q. Do quests matter?'''<br>
A. While there are many quests in EverQuest Legends, quests are not the primary way to level in the game.  Quests are beneficial for rewards, which can include gear and faction, but more experience is gained by killing monsters of an appropriate level.

'''Q. What is the best class combination?'''<br>
A. This is a highly subjective question, and there is no one best answer.  All class combinations are viable, and aside from your primary class, can be changed at will.  While not every combination may be able to clear all the content in the game, all are playable, so try different combinations to find one you enjoy.

'''Q. What are Motes, and how do I use them?'''<br>
A. Motes can be used in-game to upgrade gear and spells.  Check out the [[Mote Guide]] for more detailed information.

'''Q. Where can I buy spells?'''<br>
A. Spells can be bought from spell vendors for that class in most major cities.  Not every city has vendors for every class.  [[New Sebilis Expedition]] is a popular one as it does have vendors for every class.

